# Build-time configuration for the deployed frontend.
#
# Every value here is a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable, which Next.js inlines into the
# client bundle at build time - they are public by definition and visible to
# anyone who opens devtools. There are no secrets in this file and there must
# never be any.
#
# Committed deliberately rather than kept in the host's dashboard. Vercel stores
# CLI-added variables as "Sensitive", and sensitive variables are withheld from
# the build, so NEXT_PUBLIC_* values set that way silently fail to inline and
# the app ships pointing at nothing. Keeping them here makes the build
# reproducible and independent of dashboard state.

# The published live snapshot. This is the dashboard's only data source: there
# is no API. The file is written by `make refresh` and committed to main, so
# this URL is the main branch's copy by design.
#
# A preview built from a branch that changes the snapshot schema needs to read
# that branch's copy instead. Override at deploy time rather than editing this
# file, so no branch-specific URL is ever committed:
#
#   vercel --build-env NEXT_PUBLIC_HAZE_SNAPSHOT_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ShabriSebastian/hazewatch-ai/<branch>/data/live/latest.json
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_HAZE_SNAPSHOT_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ShabriSebastian/hazewatch-ai/main/data/live/latest.json

# The accumulated alert history. Optional: when unset it is derived from the
# snapshot URL by swapping the filename, which is correct whenever the two sit
# side by side - and they always do, because one commit writes both.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HAZE_HISTORY_URL=
